 "note": [
  "The table the Modern Hebrew time composer is held to.",
  "",
  "NOT yet read by a speaker of this language. Unlike he-IL.numbers.json,",
  "which is a fence around what has been shipping since 0.152, every row",
  "here is new: this app has told the time in no language until now, and",
  "nobody has told it how Hebrew does it. So the rows below are what the",
  "composer says given the words in `system`, and `check` marks the ones",
  "where two answers are both plausible and a speaker has to pick.",
  "",
  "Read the file this way: the words in `system` are the claim, and the",
  "rows are arithmetic over them. If a row is wrong and the words are",
  "right, the composer is wrong. If the words are wrong, a teacher fixes",
  "them on their own screen and nothing here has to change — which is the",
  "whole point of the lexicon being data.",
  "",
  "The hour comes from the number system in he-IL.numbers.json, asked for",
  "a feminine referent, because the word for hour is feminine. If the hour",
  "is ever wrong here and right there, the fault is in this file's",
  "expectations and not in the composer, which has no agreement in it."
 ],
